#4471 combines different problems. Its one-fix summary and subject-only deduplication are not reliable guides to the actual cause. The table counts unique report IDs merged into #4471 in the 4 October export. Five reports are separated by symptom for investigation; this does not establish a separate cause. The desk continues to receive and merge reports, so this is a snapshot, not a live count.

<Incident4471Split />

## Month/day parser

The shared parser reads month first even for day-first tenants. Dates such as 7 April can become 4 July. Fix parsing using the tenant's date order and add ambiguous-date tests. This investigation split excludes the five reports read as one-day moves; the export's original classification includes them as parser reports. See [issue #1](https://github.com/grzehow/MegaDev/issues/1).

## Booking form hint

The booking-v3 form tells people to enter MM/DD/YYYY even when their tenant uses day-first dates, while the form reads their entry in tenant order. Correct the hint to match the format accepted by the form and test both day-first and month-first tenants. This is not the shared parser defect. See [issue #2](https://github.com/grzehow/MegaDev/issues/2).

## Reports read as one-day moves

Five reports listed in `desk-notes.json` were read by the desk as one-day moves. They are listed separately in the table for investigation rather than double-counted. The export classifies them as parser reports, and their symptoms do not establish a separate cause. See [issue #3](https://github.com/grzehow/MegaDev/issues/3).

## Triage

Deduplicate on demonstrated cause and affected path, not subject or intake tag alone. Confirm unclear reports against the reporter and revisit counts as the desk works. The existing accepted decision record remains unchanged; replace it with a new decision if the desk adopts a new rule.

